<title>SOUTH KOREA: Two S.Korean firms say buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</title>
<headline>Two S.Korean firms say buy 22,500T of U.S. wheat.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Cheiljedang Corp and Dongah Flour Mills Co Ltd joinlty bought 22,500 tonnes of U.S. No.1 wheat from Japanese trading house Marubeni Corp, company officials said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>  Soft White		1,300   $169.02</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 5,300   $175.36</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  1,500   $180.23</p>
<p>Cheiljedang Corp</p>
<p>  Type of Wheat	   Tonne   Price/Bushel(FOB)</p>
<p>  Soft White		2,500   $0.8725 (over CBOT's Sept)</p>
<p>(ordinary)</p>
<p>  Soft White		1,000   $0.8725 (	&quot;	   )</p>
<p>(protein max 9.5 pct)</p>
<p>  Hard Red Winter	 3,000   $0.8200 (over KCBT's Sept)</p>
<p>  Dark Northern Spring  3,000   $1.0300 (over MGE's Sept)</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
